# Git push identity & repo gate (mandatory)

Before **any** `git push` (including `-u`, tags, or force), run these checks in the repo and compare outputs to the expected values. Do **not** push if any check fails — stop and report the mismatch to the user.

Canonical repository: **https://github.com/openqa-cn/codexqa.git** (`openqa-cn/codexqa`).

## Required checks (run in order)

```bash
git config user.name
# expected: leviacicig

git config user.email
# expected: eviacici@126.com

git remote -v
# expected: origin points at openqa-cn/codexqa
#   preferred SSH (this identity): git@github.com-leviacicig:openqa-cn/codexqa.git
#   also OK:                      git@github.com:openqa-cn/codexqa.git
#   also OK:                      https://github.com/openqa-cn/codexqa.git
# AND: URL host/path uses github.com-leviacicig (preferred), OR core.sshCommand
#      points at this identity's key when using github.com / HTTPS+SSH helper
# reject: placeholders such as ORG/REPO.git

ssh -T git@github.com-leviacicig
# expected: successful GitHub auth for leviacicig
#           (e.g. "Hi leviacicig! You've successfully authenticated...")
```

## Pass / fail rules

| Check | Pass when | Fail when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `user.name` | Exact string `leviacicig` | Empty, different, or missing |
| `user.email` | Exact string `eviacici@126.com` | Empty, different, or missing |
| `remote -v` repo | Fetch/push URL path is `openqa-cn/codexqa` (`.git` optional) | Wrong owner/repo, `ORG/REPO`, or missing origin |
| `remote -v` / SSH identity | URL uses `github.com-leviacicig`, **or** `core.sshCommand` uses this identity's key | Neither condition holds |
| `ssh -T` | Auth succeeds as `leviacicig` | Permission denied, wrong user, host unreachable, or no success message |

## On failure

1. **Do not** run `git push` (or any equivalent that updates the remote).
2. Report which check failed, show **expected vs actual**, and wait for the user.
3. Do not rewrite global git config unless the user explicitly asks.
4. If only the remote URL is wrong, you may set  
   `git remote set-url origin git@github.com-leviacicig:openqa-cn/codexqa.git`  
   **after** confirming with the user, then re-run the gate before push.

## On success

Only then may you push to `origin` on the current branch (e.g. `leviacicig-dev`).
